 "notes": "CAPP-12TB haloscope, DFSZ-sensitive axion DM search over m_a=4.51-4.59 ueV (nu~1.09-1.11 GHz). Headline curve is the blue 'This Work' 90% CL exclusion in Fig.4, whose y-axis is the ratio |g_gamma^CAPP/g_gamma^DFSZ|. Extracted by rendering the vector EPS (CAPP-12TB-limits-pub-v7.eps) to raster and tracing the blue line center per column (axis calibrated on the 4.52/4.54/4.56/4.58 ueV and 0.9/1.0/1.1/1.2 ratio ticks). Converted to g_agamma = ratio * g_agamma^DFSZ(m_a) with g_agamma^DFSZ = alpha*g_gamma/(pi*f_a), g_gamma=0.36, alpha=1/137.036, and f_a=1e12 GeV*(5.7 ueV/m_a) from m_a=5.7 ueV*(1e12 GeV/f_a). This reproduces the abstract's minimum g_agamma~6.2e-16 GeV^-1 (my extracted min 5.8e-16, median 6.2e-16). rho_a=0.45 GeV/cm^3 (100% DM assumed; NOT rescaled). Narrow upward spikes are less-sensitive frequencies (filtering/mode crossing at 4.527 ueV); curve traces the line center. A separate KSVZ-density limit (Fig.5) is not the headline.",
